    "captured": false,
    "note": "WRITTEN, NOT CAPTURED. Each payload is built key-for-key from the payload builders in OAraLabs/Prometheus src/prometheus/computer/livestream.py (ComputerLiveStream.binding / task_started / step / task_ended / _emit's stream-error path) and the reply in src/prometheus/web/ws_server.py (computer_task_stop -> computer_task_stop_ack), at 6be4020 on claude/cu-v11-pr6-cockpit (draft PR #663). The envelope is ws_server's {type, timestamp (epoch seconds), payload}. No daemon running #663 was reachable when this was written. Replace it with a capture taken at window.beacon.events.onGateway once one is, as src/main/fixtures/coding-wire-c941664a6.json was. The computer_step_thumbnail frame and the thumbnail/thumbnail_skip_reason fields on computer_step are likewise WRITTEN, key-for-key from OAraLabs/Prometheus src/prometheus/computer/thumbnails.py (build_frame/FRAME_KEYS) and livestream.py step(), at PR #701 (merged 1b87e2e). Still not captured from a live daemon: computer_use is off, and re-capturing is plan step 2.1.",
    "layer1": "Layer-1 frames (tool_call_start/end for computer_task and computer_<verb>, agent_progress, chat_done) also arrive while a task runs. They are already decoded by the chat path and are not computer_* kinds, so the scenarios leave them out. task_layer1_end holds the two that close the 'task' scenario (livestream.py task_ended), so smoke:computer can check they stay out of the computer state: the chat_done carries message_id \"computer:<task_id>\", a string handle and never a rowid (no row_id key), since 6be4020.",
    "scenarios": {
      "task": "A whole task: the person's app pick turns on for one task, the task starts, a click runs under the pick, a Return press waits on an approval and then runs, the chooser finds nothing more to do, the task ends done, and the pick turns off.",
      "stopped": "A Stop mid-task: this socket sends computer_task_stop, gets the ack, the click already dispatched lands after the stop (in_flight_at_stop), and the task ends stopped.",
      "log_failed": "One step's frame was not delivered. The daemon numbered it (seq 2) before the emit failed, so seq 2 never arrives and a computer_stream_error names the task instead. The task itself carries on."
    }
  },
